## 10. Best Practices Checklist

### Schema Design
- ✅ Use meaningful model and field names
- ✅ Add indexes for frequently queried fields
- ✅ Use enums for fixed value sets
- ✅ Include timestamps (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`)
- ✅ Define proper relations with `onDelete` cascades
- ✅ Use `@@index` for compound queries

### Client Usage
- ✅ Use singleton pattern for PrismaClient
- ✅ Close connections in serverless functions
- ✅ Use transactions for multi-step operations
- ✅ Leverage `include` and `select` to control data fetching
- ✅ Implement pagination for large datasets

### Migrations
- ✅ Never edit migration files manually
- ✅ Use descriptive migration names
- ✅ Test migrations on staging before production
- ✅ Keep migration history in version control
- ✅ Use `prisma migrate deploy` in CI/CD

### Performance
- ✅ Avoid N+1 queries with proper `include`
- ✅ Use connection pooling for serverless
- ✅ Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- ✅ Monitor query performance with Prisma Optimize
- ✅ Use `select` to fetch only needed fields

### Security
- ✅ Never expose raw database URLs in code
- ✅ Use environment variables for credentials
- ✅ Validate input before database operations
- ✅ Implement proper error handling
- ✅ Use row-level security where appropriate

